// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/sar_comparator_q.t27 -- the SAR ADC dynamic comparator with the devices' own charge and the body effect: PSP103 tables at 27 C, judged by ngspice
; M4b-q of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #11312). M4b (specs/analog/sar_comparator.t27) solves the golden SAR deck's StrongARM latch, eight nodes, by a multi-node Newton step; M4b-psp
; (sar_comparator_psp.t27) ran it on the PSP103 current tables at 50 C and found the decision 98 times too fast against ngspice with all its charge, "until the charge tables exist". They exist now: the drain and
; gate charge of both devices (M3c, TT_QD_N, TT_QG_N, TT_QD_P, TT_QG_P), the log-domain current tables (M3c-2) and their source-to-bulk axis (M3e). This file puts the three into the comparator at 27 C, the
; report's temperature, with the same backward Euler charge step as the 500 fF inverter of M3c, and judges the decision time against ngspice-47 running the same comparator. The solver is reused, not copied:
; sar_comparator.t27's sc_stamp_chan is split in two and the second half, `sc_stamp_chan_w` (the stamp of a channel whose current and slopes are already read), is the stamp used here, with a fourth slope added (along
; the source-to-bulk voltage; 0 for every old caller, so the 20 tests and the pinned folds of sar_comparator.t27 are unchanged); the elimination, the back substitution, the registers and the sign-magnitude
; words are M4b's. Everything else is here.
; -
; WHAT WAS ASKED AND WHAT CAME OUT, first. The issue asks for a 27 C comparator with the devices' charge and the body effect whose decision time at +2 mV and -2 mV is within 10 percent of ngspice's own run of the same
; comparator at 27 C. It is: 613.07 ps and 613.15 ps against ngspice's 602.54 ps, +1.75 and +1.76 percent (the bar is 10); +1.62 percent against ngspice's backward Euler on the model's own 1.6 ps grid; +1.00 percent against the
; external team's report of 2026-10-16 (607 ps). The model of M4b-psp, with no charge, was 5.4 ps. The first model built to the letter of the issue (the drain and gate charge from the tables, the source terminal's the
; remainder so that the four charges add to zero) did not converge: the bulk's charge, 4 to 7 percent of the gate's, landed on the source node and jumped when the two ends of a channel exchanged their parts, and the
; last Newton residual stays at 1.9e6 units (0.11 V). The source terminal is therefore closed by its two edges (THE SOURCE CHARGE below), which the tables give exactly, and that is the one step beyond the issue.
; -
; THE REFERENCE. The comparator is written out, not read: the thirteen sg13_lv transistors of the golden dynamic_comparator and its inverter, with the W, L and m of sar_cmp_psp_r2b.cir (facts of the circuit, none of the
; golden deck's text), the bulks as the golden deck has them (every NMOS on ground, every PMOS on VDD), 4 fF on dp and dn, an ideal 1.6 ps clock, PSP103 of the IHP-Open-PDK 21133f21 (mos_tt) through ngspice-47 and OSDI, on the
; reference host. THAT NETLIST IS THE GOLDEN COMPARATOR: at 50 C and the golden deck's start it gives the first output through 0.75 V 523.032, 528.006, 529.386 and 529.741 ps after the clock, the four numbers
; the golden subcircuit gave in sar_cmp_psp_real.cir (sar_cmp_q_ref50.cir; a test). Three starts, because the start is not nothing:
;   the golden deck's    the initial conditions with uic and the clock at 200 ps: the nodes inside the PSP103 devices start at 0 V, their first charging disturbs the others (n_clkc falls to 0.56 V in 10 ps, ap, an, net2, net3 are
;                        kicked over the supply, dp and dn rise to 0.9 V) and 200 ps do not settle it (at the clock n_clkc is 1.30 V, dp and dn 0.62 V). Its decision time is 508.1 ps at 27 C, 523.0 ps at 50 C: numbers of that
;                        start. The 98 times of M4b-psp are against it.
;   the SETTLED start    sar_cmp_q_ref.cir RUN S: the spec's rest (ap = an = net2 = net3 = n_clkc = 1.5 V, dp = dn = 0, net1 = max(VDP, VDN) - 0.35 V) as .ic WITHOUT uic, so that ngspice solves the DC operating point with the
;                        eight nodes forced and the devices' internal nodes consistent, then releases them, the clock at 1 ps. This is the model's start and the reference of the issue: 602.54 ps at 27 C, 632.56 ps at 50 C.
;   the FREE start       sar_cmp_q_free.cir: the operating point with the clock low and net1, which no switch resets, where the leakage of the pair and of the tail balance (0.7073 V): 607.145 ps, the external team's report
;                        to 0.02 percent. The model can start from it too (sq_rest takes a word for net1).
; The trapezoidal run is ngspice's default with the step capped at 0.5 ps; sar_cmp_q_be.cir is its backward Euler (gear, maxord 1) on a fixed grid of 0.2, 0.4, 0.8 and 1.6 ps with the clock a step of the grid, the scheme of the model:
; the decision time is within 0.01, 0.02, 0.10 and 0.13 percent of the trapezoidal one, so the model's one step of 1.6 ps is not an error of the scheme at the resolution of this comparison.
; -
; THE MODEL. The state is the eight nodes of sar_comparator.t27 (ap, an, net1, net2, net3, dp, dn, n_clkc), voltages in words of 2^-24 V with ground 0.5 V up the range (SQ_OFF), so that a node can go 0.5 V below ground
; (n_clkc and net1 do, by 0.36 and 0.23 V in ngspice and 0.40 and 0.28 V in the model, when the clock falls) and 1 V above the supply (ap and an do, by 0.39 V, when it rises). The step is 1.6 ps and the clock is a step of the grid: 438 steps cover 700 ps. The charge unit is 2 fF
; and a current word is the current in IUNIT (1.164 pA) over 64, so dt / C is the 800 V/A of M4b. A device of the fifteen is read at its two channel ends (the higher is the drain of an NMOS and the source of a PMOS), its gate
; drive x and its Vds y, the bulk of an NMOS on ground and of a PMOS on the supply (the golden netlist's), so the source-to-bulk voltage Vsb is the low end above ground for an NMOS and the supply above the high end for a PMOS.
;   the current    the log-domain tables TT_LG_N and TT_LG_P read on the source-to-bulk axis (vsb_fine of mos_psp103_vsb_data.t27, seven slices, the log word blended between two); the slopes are forward differences of the same
;                  reads over 1 mV along the gate, Vds and Vsb (a rise of the low end of an NMOS lowers the current by gm + gds + gmb, a rise of the high end of a PMOS raises it by the same), so that value and slope are one
;                  object (FR-002 of M3c); a device whose gate is beyond its source has no gate slope.
;   the charge     the terminal charges of the device at (x, y) from the M3c tables, read by the bilinear read of M3a and sloped off the same cell (the drain charge QD, the gate charge QG, the PMOS tables negated); the
;                  node charge is the sum of the terminals at the node, and the backward Euler equation of a node is the M3c one, G = (Q(v) - Q(v0)) + (currents out - currents in), with Q(v0) of the previous step's state and clock
;                  (the clock edge is a jump of charge, as the gate edge of the 500 fF inverter). The tables stop at 0 and 1.5 V on both axes; beyond them the charge goes on linearly with the slope of the edge cell, so the charge
;                  and the slope the Newton step uses are one function (a node kicked 0.39 V over the supply, a gate drive of 1.75 V, a gate beyond its source: the gate overlap and the accumulation). The lumped capacitors are the
;                  real circuit's, 4 fF on dp and dn, and nothing else.
;   THE SOURCE CHARGE  the tables hold the drain and the gate terminal, with source and bulk tied; the source terminal is the remainder, Qs = -(Qd + Qg) - Qb, and the bulk's charge Qb is not tabulated. It is closed by its two edges,
;                  Qb(x, y) = Qb(x, 0) + Qb(0, y) with Qb(x, 0) = -(Qg + 2 Qd)(x, 0) (the device is symmetric at Vds = 0, so Qs = Qd there) and Qb(0, y) = -(Qd + Qg)(0, y) (the source is untouched while the channel is off):
;                  Qs(x, 0) = Qd(x, 0) and Qs(0, y) = 0 EXACTLY, a test for both devices, so the charge does not jump when the two ends of a channel exchange their roles, and Qs in the interior is the tables' charge without the
;                  bulk's variation along both axes at once (the cross term, which is small: Qb is 4 percent of Qg at a gate drive of 1.5 V on an NMOS, 7 percent on a PMOS). Without it (SQ_M_NOCLOSURE, Qs = -(Qd + Qg)) the last Newton residual
;                  is 1.88e6 units (0.11 V) and the time it reads is 544 ps, nothing.
;   the step       backward Euler on the eight nodes at once, K = 4 Newton iterations from the previous state, the eight-by-eight pivoted elimination in sign-magnitude words of sar_comparator.t27 (sc_load, sc_eliminate,
;                  sc_backsub, sc_apply_lim with the top of the range at 1 V over the supply), the residual after the last iteration computed at every step as the Newton move still owed, in units (59.6 nV).
; -
; THE RESULT, K = 4, tt 27 C, times in ps after the clock's 50 percent point (the first output through 0.75 V), ngspice the settled start:
;   input          model      ngspice     gap         ngspice BE 1.6 ps   gap
;   +2 mV          613.074    602.537    +1.75 %      603.316            +1.62 %
;   -2 mV          613.151    602.537    +1.76 %
;   +0.5 mV        624.138    608.023    +2.65 %      609.012            +2.48 %
;   0.125 mV       627.716    609.602    +2.97 %
;   31 uV          628.686    610.014    +3.06 %
;   10 uV          629.046    610.108    +3.10 %
;   1 uV, 0.12 uV  629.114, 629.090   610.148, 610.152   +3.11 %, +3.10 %
;   free start     614.860    607.145    +1.27 %      (the report, 607 ps: +1.29 %)   0.5 mV: +2.15 %, 31 uV: +2.56 %
; so the decision time is between 1.75 and 3.11 percent over ngspice's at every input, the same sign, a third of the 10 percent. The sign is right at +-2 mV; below 10 uV the model's decision is the rounding's (it
; depends on K and on the least bit of the tables), which is the flip point of a symmetric latch at the resolution of 59.6 nV and 1 mV forward differences, and no claim is made there. THE LEVELS after the decision, at 2 ns:
; dp 1.49933 V and dn 2.26 mV against ngspice's 1.49884 V and 2.283 mV (0.49 mV and 0.02 mV). THE RESET, the clock falling at 2 ns: 1.4 ns later (3.4 ns) every node is within 2.6 mV of ngspice's, dp and dn
; are 3.08 mV and -0.17 mV against 3.265 mV and -0.247 mV (0.19 mV and 0.08 mV); in the 400 ps after the fall, while the nodes swing through volts, the model is 51 mV off on the outputs at the worst, 0.18 V on ap
; and 0.31 V on net2 (which recovers faster in the model), and the fall step itself kicks the nodes 10 to 40 percent further than ngspice's grid does (ap -0.24 V against -0.17 V, n_clkc -0.40 V against
; -0.36 V). THE RESOLUTION TIME (|dp - dn| through 0.75 V), not a row of the report, is 1040.7 ps against 1094.3 ps, 4.9 percent early: the regeneration is faster in the model.
; -
; THE ERRORS, kept apart.
;   arithmetic   the last Newton residual is at most 706 units (42 uV) over the 438 steps of a short run and 1545 units (0.09 mV) over the 2125 steps of the long run, the clock-fall step included. K = 3 to 8 give the
;                decision time 613.07 to 613.15 ps, so the iteration count does not matter above 3; K = 2 leaves 2.76e5 units at the clock edge (a test refuses it by the residual, not by the time, which is 612.99 ps) and K = 1
;                3.3e6. There is no real-arithmetic twin of the iteration in this file: the claim is the residual and the stability of the answer.
;   the Jacobian is the derivative of the residual to 1.5 percent of the diagonal of its row (a central difference of the residual over 1 mV, the largest of the 64 entries, at the clock edge and at four states of the
;                run), the transposed matrix is off by more than 0.2 (tests); the forward differences of the current and the chords of the cells are the 1.5 percent.
;   table/model  the model against ngspice's backward Euler on the same 1.6 ps grid, all the nodes: at the 13 times of the rows, from 50 to 500 ps (ahead of the decision) the largest distance is 27.1 mV (ap, an:
;                the model discharges them 1 to 2 percent early; net1 is within 3 mV, n_clkc within 10 mV, dp and dn within 8 mV), up to 1.5 ns (through the regeneration) 83.4 mV (dp and dn at the resolution edge, 4.9 percent
;                early in time); at the clock edge ap is 80.9 mV off at the 50 percent point of the clock and 58 mV at the top of its kick, 10 ps later (the kick is 0.39 V in ngspice and 0.45 V in the model; the cause is not
;                isolated: the same grid and the same step as ngspice's backward Euler, the model's charge is the tables' and their closure).
;   body effect  the source-to-bulk axis is worth 7.4 percent of the decision time: without it (SQ_M_NOBODY, Vsb forced to 0, the 2-D read) the decision is 570.6 ps, 5.30 percent UNDER ngspice's, inside the bar of 10 percent
;                and outside a bar of 3: the control is the model's gap with the body effect, +1.75 percent, against -5.30 without, three times as far. The body effect on the CHARGE is not in the model (the charge tables have the bulk
;                tied to the source): the junction charge of the source ends of XM3, XM4 (net1 is 0.15 to 0.5 V above their bulk) and of XM8, XM9, and the shift of their threshold, are in no table.
;   scheme       ngspice backward Euler on the 1.6 ps grid against its trapezoidal run: +0.13 percent (decision), -0.33 percent (resolution); shared by construction.
; -
; THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS, tests that pass by seeing the failure:
;   charge removed        the devices' own charge off and the lumped capacitors of the square-law model (4, 4, 6, 2, 2, 4, 4, 2 fF) on every node: 5.40 ps, 111 times too fast, under the report's lower limit of 10 ps and 99 percent
;                         under ngspice. At this step the no-charge latch does not even regenerate (both outputs sit at 0.786 V from 50 ps on: the backward Euler step of 1.6 ps is several times the time
;                         constant of a circuit without its charge), so the 5.40 ps is the common-mode rise, which is what the old model's 5.35 ps was too; the control is judged by the time.
;   no body effect        570.6 ps, above.
;   no closure            the Newton step does not converge (1.88e6 units), above.
;   charge tables swapped the PMOS tables for the NMOS devices and the reverse: the nodes run to the top of the range, 4.2e9 units of residual, 7.8 ps.
;   K = 2, K = 1          2.76e5 and 3.3e6 units of residual.
;   inputs exchanged      the sign flips and the time is the same to 0.08 ps.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The comparator of eight nodes and fifteen devices, each read from the tt 27 C PSP103 log tables on the source-to-bulk axis with its drain, gate and source charge from the M3c tables and the closure above, solved by
; backward Euler of 1.6 ps with four Newton iterations (last residual at most 1545 units), decides +-2 mV the right way; its decision time is 613.07 ps and 613.15 ps, within 1.76 percent of ngspice-47 on the golden comparator at
; the settled start (the bar is 10 percent) and within 3.11 percent over the whole range of inputs, inside the report's 10 ps to 10 ns; its end levels at 2 ns and its reset level at 3.4 ns (the clock falling at 2 ns) are within
; 0.5 mV of ngspice's; the charge removed, the closure removed, the tables in the wrong slots and too few iterations are each refused. WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. The resolution time (4.9 percent early) and the nodes in the
; regeneration (up to 83 mV) and during the reset (30 to 60 mV) are the model's own and are not within the bar of the decision time. Nothing about the body effect on the charge, the closure beyond its two exact edges
; (a deck that prints the source terminal's charge would test it), another corner or temperature (tt 27 C only: the 50 C tables have no charge and no source-to-bulk axis), noise, mismatch, another W, L or supply; the
; converter's comparator (its delay-cell clock, the kickback of its input stages, the NAND "Valid" and the inverters x5, x6 are not here); the flip point of the isolated latch below 10 uV; hardware: the functions from sq_clk_at
; to sq_run take and return unsigned words and sign-magnitude words and have no float, and no board top, clock, LUT, DSP, BRAM, Fmax or UART line is claimed. The golden deck is not in this repository (its comparator is
; written out in the decks); the reference host's runs are the numbers below. ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogSarComparatorQ;

use analog::linear::{fold, fabs64};
use analog::mos_table::{VDD, CELL_BITS, lim, cell_of, frac_of, node_at, dpos, blend1, id_of, mag_diff};
use analog::mos_psp103_data::{TT_LG_N, TT_LG_P, TT_QD_N, TT_QG_N, TT_QD_P, TT_QG_P};
use analog::mos_psp103_vsb_data::{vsb_fine};
use analog::sar_comparator_psp::{NG_RL_FIRST_PS, sp_rel};
use analog::sar_comparator::{SC_CAP, SC_NN, SC_DP, SC_DN, SC_NDEV, SC_RJP, SC_RJN, SC_DV_KIND, SC_DV_D, SC_DV_G, SC_DV_S, SC_DV_M, SC_T_VDD, SC_T_GND, SC_T_CLK, SC_T_VDP, SC_T_VDN, SC_RGP, SC_RGN, SC_VCM, SC_VTH_U, SC_QB, SC_NONE, sc_stamp_chan_w, sc_add_j, sc_clear, sc_stamp_cap, sc_resid, sc_load, sc_eliminate, sc_backsub, sc_apply_lim, sc_pack, sc_neg, sc_mag, sc_sadd, sc_flip};

pub const KIND : str = "analog-cell";
pub const ID : str = "analog/sar_comparator_q";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "the golden SAR deck's dynamic_comparator (GPL-2.0, read at run time, never vendored; written out in specs/analog/decks/sar_cmp_q_ref.cir); IHP-Open-PDK 21133f21 PSP103 through ngspice-47, 27 C";

; --- the units ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Ground, in words: every voltage of the run carries 2^23 units (0.5 V) of offset, so that a node may go below ground (the outputs do by 70 mV when the clock rises and the nodes by 0.36 V when it falls)
/// and above the supply (the precharge nodes go 0.39 V above it).
pub const SQ_OFF : u32 = 8388608;
/// The supply: 1.5 V above ground.
pub const SQ_VDD : u32 = 33554432;
/// The highest a node may go: 1 V above the supply.
pub const SQ_TOP : u32 = 50331648;
/// The step: 1.6 ps; the charge unit: 2 fF; so dt / C_unit = 800 V/A, a current word is the current in IUNIT over 64.
pub const SQ_DT_FS : u32 = 1600;
pub const SQ_CU_AF : u32 = 2000;
/// A charge table word is Q / 500 fF in units of 2^-24 V, so it is 500 fF / 2 fF = 250 words of this solver's charge.
pub const SQ_QS : u64 = 250;
/// 4 fF on dp and dn, in charge units: the real circuit's only lumped capacitors.
pub const SQ_C4 : u64 = 2;
/// The lumped capacitances of the square-law model of sar_comparator.t27 in charge units of 2 fF (4, 4, 6, 2, 2, 4, 4, 2 fF on ap an net1 net2 net3 dp dn n_clkc): the model of the devices without their charge.
pub const SQ_CAP_M4B : [8]u64 = [2, 2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1];
/// The origin offset of the charge tables, 2^21.
pub const SQ_QOFF : u32 = 2097152;
/// The step, in units, of the difference that reads a slope of a current off the table: 2^14 (1 mV). A slope per cell (2^20 units) in current words is then the difference of the two reads in IUNIT itself
/// (2^20 / 2^14 = 64 is the factor between an IUNIT and a current word).
pub const SQ_DV : u32 = 16384;
/// The clock rises in SQ_R steps (1.6 ps, one step: the edge is a step of the grid, and ngspice's backward Euler on the same grid is the reference of the scheme).
pub const SQ_R : u32 = 1;
/// Newton iterations of a step: K = 3 to 8 give the decision time 613.07 to 613.15 ps; four leave at most 1545 units (0.09 mV) at all 2125 steps of the long run.
pub const SQ_K : u32 = 4;
/// The short run: 438 steps, 700.8 ps, past the decision of every input down to 1 unit. The long run: the clock falls at step SQ_JF (2 ns) and the run goes on to step SQ_NL (3.4 ns), 1.4 ns into the reset.
pub const SQ_NS : u32 = 438;
pub const SQ_JF : u32 = 1250;
pub const SQ_NL : u32 = 2125;

/// The bar of the cross-check with ngspice: a decision time within 10 percent of ngspice's own run of the same circuit (mos_psp103_gates.t27's GT_B_REL); a level within 5 mV, a tenth of the report's 50 mV.
pub const SQ_BAR : f64 = 0.10;
pub const SQ_BAR_LEVEL_V : f64 = 0.005;

; --- the modes of a run: the model, and the four ways of breaking it that the negative controls use ------------------------------------------------
pub const SQ_M_NOCHARGE : u32 = 1;
pub const SQ_M_NOBODY : u32 = 2;
pub const SQ_M_NOCLOSURE : u32 = 4;
pub const SQ_M_SWAPQ : u32 = 8;

; --- the circuit -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// The clock at step j, in words: low at step 0, rising over SQ_R steps, and when jf is not 0 falling over SQ_R steps from step jf (the reset phase).
pub fn sq_clk_at(j: u32, jf: u32) -> u32 {
    if (jf > 0 and j >= jf) {
        const i : u32 = j - jf + 1;
        if (i >= SQ_R) { return SQ_OFF; }
        return SQ_VDD - i * (VDD / SQ_R);
    }
    if (j >= SQ_R) { return SQ_VDD; }
    return SQ_OFF + j * (VDD / SQ_R);
}

pub fn sq_term_v(tm: u32, v: []const u32, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32) -> u32 {
    if (tm < SC_NN) { return v[tm as usize]; }
    if (tm == SC_T_VDD) { return SQ_VDD; }
    if (tm == SC_T_GND) { return SQ_OFF; }
    if (tm == SC_T_CLK) { return clk; }
    if (tm == SC_T_VDP) { return vdp; }
    return vdn;
}

pub fn sq_cur_tab(kind: u32) -> []const u32 {
    if (kind == 0) { return &TT_LG_N; }
    return &TT_LG_P;
}

pub fn sq_qd_tab(kind: u32) -> []const u32 {
    if (kind == 0) { return &TT_QD_N; }
    return &TT_QD_P;
}

pub fn sq_qg_tab(kind: u32) -> []const u32 {
    if (kind == 0) { return &TT_QG_N; }
    return &TT_QG_P;
}

; --- signed words ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// w * k.
pub fn sq_mul(w: u64, k: u64) -> u64 {
    return sc_pack(sc_mag(w) * k, sc_neg(w));
}

/// The signed charge of a table word relative to the table's origin: the word less 2^21 for an NMOS table, the negation of that for a PMOS table (stored negated).
pub fn sq_qw(w: u32, pmos: bool) -> u64 {
    if (w >= SQ_QOFF) { return sc_pack((w - SQ_QOFF) as u64, pmos); }
    return sc_pack((SQ_QOFF - w) as u64, !pmos);
}

/// The slope of a table along an axis (0: the first argument, 1: the second) in words per cell, its rising part (neg false) or its falling part (neg true), read off the same cell as `id_of`
/// reads the value: the cell's difference along the axis, blended along the other.
pub fn sq_tslope(t: []const u32, vg: u32, vd: u32, axis: u32, fall: bool) -> u64 {
    const gv : u32 = lim(vg);
    const dv : u32 = lim(vd);
    const cx : u32 = cell_of(gv);
    const cy : u32 = cell_of(dv);
    var a0 : u64 = 0;
    var a1 : u64 = 0;
    var b0 : u64 = 0;
    var b1 : u64 = 0;
    var f : u32 = 0;
    if (axis == 0) {
        a0 = node_at(t, cx, cy);
        a1 = node_at(t, cx + 1, cy);
        b0 = node_at(t, cx, cy + 1);
        b1 = node_at(t, cx + 1, cy + 1);
        f = frac_of(dv);
    } else {
        a0 = node_at(t, cx, cy);
        a1 = node_at(t, cx, cy + 1);
        b0 = node_at(t, cx + 1, cy);
        b1 = node_at(t, cx + 1, cy + 1);
        f = frac_of(gv);
    }
    if (fall) { return blend1(dpos(a0, a1), dpos(b0, b1), f) as u64; }
    return blend1(dpos(a1, a0), dpos(b1, b0), f) as u64;
}

/// The signed slope of the charge of a device along an axis, words per cell: the rising part less the falling part of the table, negated for a PMOS table.
pub fn sq_slope(t: []const u32, vg: u32, vd: u32, axis: u32, pmos: bool) -> u64 {
    const up : u64 = sc_pack(sq_tslope(t, vg, vd, axis, false), pmos);
    const dn : u64 = sc_pack(sq_tslope(t, vg, vd, axis, true), !pmos);
    return sc_sadd(up, dn);
}

/// The signed charge of a device at the gate drive x (xn units below the source when negative, so the table is read at 0) and Vds y, from the table t (words relative to the origin, negated for a PMOS
/// table). The table covers 0 .. 1.5 V on both axes; the charge goes on beyond its edges linearly with the slope of the edge cell, so that the charge and the slope the Newton step uses are one function:
/// below the source (xn > 0, the gate beyond a channel end: the overlap and the accumulation), above the supply (a node kicked over the rail, a gate drive of more than 1.5 V: x or y above VDD).
pub fn sq_qt(t: []const u32, x: u32, xn: u32, y: u32, pmos: bool) -> u64 {
    var q : u64 = sq_qw(id_of(t, x, y), pmos);
    if (xn > 0) {
        const s0 : u64 = sq_slope(t, 0, y, 0, pmos);
        q = sc_sadd(q, sc_pack((sc_mag(s0) * (xn as u64)) >> CELL_BITS, !sc_neg(s0)));
    }
    if (x > VDD) {
        const sx : u64 = sq_slope(t, VDD, y, 0, pmos);
        q = sc_sadd(q, sc_pack((sc_mag(sx) * ((x - VDD) as u64)) >> CELL_BITS, sc_neg(sx)));
    }
    if (y > VDD) {
        const sy : u64 = sq_slope(t, x, VDD, 1, pmos);
        q = sc_sadd(q, sc_pack((sc_mag(sy) * ((y - VDD) as u64)) >> CELL_BITS, sc_neg(sy)));
    }
    return q;
}

/// The source terminal's charge (or slope) from the drain's and the gate's, the four terminal charges adding to zero and the bulk's charge closed by its two edges: Qb(x, y) = Qb(x, 0) + Qb(0, y) with
/// Qb(x, 0) = -(Qg + 2 Qd)(x, 0) (the device symmetric at Vds = 0, so Qs = Qd there) and Qb(0, y) = -(Qd + Qg)(0, y) (the source untouched while the channel is off). It gives Qs(x, 0) = Qd(x, 0) and
/// Qs(0, y) = 0 exactly, so the charge does not jump when the two ends of a channel exchange their parts, and it is the two-table closure of Qs; qd, qg are read at (x, y), qd0x, qg0x at (x, 0), qd0y, qg0y at (0, y).
pub fn sq_qsrc(qd: u64, qg: u64, qd0x: u64, qg0x: u64, qd0y: u64, qg0y: u64) -> u64 {
    return sc_sadd(sc_sadd(sc_flip(sc_sadd(qd, qg)), sc_sadd(sc_sadd(qd0x, qd0x), qg0x)), sc_sadd(qd0y, qg0y));
}

/// The node charges: add the signed word w to the positive or negative accumulator of node n (terminals above the eight nodes have none).
pub fn sq_acc(qa: []u64, n: u32, w: u64) {
    if (n >= SC_NN) { return; }
    if (sc_neg(w)) {
        qa[(SC_NN + n) as usize] = qa[(SC_NN + n) as usize] + sc_mag(w);
    } else {
        qa[n as usize] = qa[n as usize] + sc_mag(w);
    }
}

/// Add the signed word w to the Jacobian entry (r, c).
pub fn sq_jadd(reg: []u64, r: u32, c: u32, w: u64) {
    sc_add_j(reg, r, c, sc_mag(w), sc_neg(w));
}

/// The charge slopes of one terminal of a device into row r: (sx, sy) per cell along the gate drive and along Vds, scaled. An NMOS reads x = Vg - Vlow, y = Vhigh - Vlow; a PMOS x = Vhigh - Vg, y = Vhigh - Vlow.
pub fn sq_jq(reg: []u64, kind: u32, r: u32, g: u32, hi: u32, lo: u32, sx: u64, sy: u64) {
    if (kind == 0) {
        sq_jadd(reg, r, g, sx);
        sq_jadd(reg, r, hi, sy);
        sq_jadd(reg, r, lo, sc_flip(sc_sadd(sx, sy)));
    } else {
        sq_jadd(reg, r, g, sc_flip(sx));
        sq_jadd(reg, r, hi, sc_sadd(sx, sy));
        sq_jadd(reg, r, lo, sc_flip(sy));
    }
}

; --- the current ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// The current of a device of kind, in IUNIT, read on the source-to-bulk axis.
pub fn sq_i(kind: u32, x: u32, y: u32, vsb: u32) -> u64 {
    return vsb_fine(kind, sq_cur_tab(kind), x, y, vsb);
}

/// The rise of the current over SQ_DV along an axis (0: gate drive, 1: Vds) in IUNIT, forward when there is room below the supply, backward otherwise; axis 2: the fall of the current over a rise of
/// the source-to-bulk voltage.
pub fn sq_fd(kind: u32, x: u32, y: u32, vsb: u32, i0: u64, axis: u32) -> u64 {
    if (axis == 0) {
        if (x + SQ_DV <= VDD) { return dpos(sq_i(kind, x + SQ_DV, y, vsb), i0); }
        return dpos(i0, sq_i(kind, x - SQ_DV, y, vsb));
    }
    if (axis == 1) {
        if (y + SQ_DV <= VDD) { return dpos(sq_i(kind, x, y + SQ_DV, vsb), i0); }
        return dpos(i0, sq_i(kind, x, y - SQ_DV, vsb));
    }
    if (vsb + SQ_DV <= VDD) { return dpos(i0, sq_i(kind, x, y, vsb + SQ_DV)); }
    return dpos(sq_i(kind, x, y, vsb - SQ_DV), i0);
}

; --- one device ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Device e at the state v with the clock clk: its terminal charges go into qa (positive terms in words 0 .. 7, negative in words 8 .. 15); with jac its current and the slopes of its current and of
/// its charges go into reg as well. The channel runs between its two ends, the higher end being the drain of an NMOS and the source of a PMOS; the NMOS bulk is ground and the PMOS bulk is the
/// supply (the golden netlist's), so the source-to-bulk voltage is the low end above ground for an NMOS and the supply above the high end for a PMOS. The charge is read at the gate drive and
/// Vds: the drain and the gate from the tables of mos_psp103_data.t27, the source terminal closed by its two edges (`sq_qsrc`; mode SQ_M_NOCLOSURE: the remainder, the bulk's charge taken as zero). The modes: see SQ_M_*.
pub fn sq_dev(e: usize, v: []const u32, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, mode: u32, jac: bool, reg: []u64, qa: []u64) {
    const kind : u32 = SC_DV_KIND[e];
    const d : u32 = SC_DV_D[e];
    const g : u32 = SC_DV_G[e];
    const s : u32 = SC_DV_S[e];
    const m : u64 = (SC_DV_M[e]) as u64;
    const vd : u32 = sq_term_v(d, v, clk, vdp, vdn);
    const vg : u32 = sq_term_v(g, v, clk, vdp, vdn);
    const vs : u32 = sq_term_v(s, v, clk, vdp, vdn);
    var hi : u32 = d;
    var lo : u32 = s;
    var vhi : u32 = vd;
    var vlo : u32 = vs;
    if (vd < vs) {
        hi = s;
        lo = d;
        vhi = vs;
        vlo = vd;
    }
    var x : u32 = 0;
    var xn : u32 = 0;
    var vsb : u32 = 0;
    var forward : bool = false;
    if (kind == 0) {
        if (vg > vlo) { x = vg - vlo; } else { xn = vlo - vg; }
        if (vlo > SQ_OFF) { vsb = vlo - SQ_OFF; } else { forward = true; }
    } else {
        if (vhi > vg) { x = vhi - vg; } else { xn = vg - vhi; }
        if (vhi < SQ_VDD) { vsb = SQ_VDD - vhi; } else { forward = true; }
    }
    if ((mode & SQ_M_NOBODY) != 0) {
        vsb = 0;
        forward = true;
    }
    const y : u32 = vhi - vlo;
    if (jac) {
        const i0 : u64 = sq_i(kind, x, y, vsb);
        var a : u64 = 0;
        if (xn == 0) { a = m * sq_fd(kind, x, y, vsb, i0, 0); }
        const b : u64 = m * sq_fd(kind, x, y, vsb, i0, 1);
        var cb : u64 = 0;
        if (!forward) { cb = m * sq_fd(kind, x, y, vsb, i0, 2); }
        sc_stamp_chan_w(kind, hi, lo, g, (m * i0 + 32) >> 6, a, b, cb, reg);
    }
    if ((mode & SQ_M_NOCHARGE) != 0) { return; }
    var kq : u32 = kind;
    if ((mode & SQ_M_SWAPQ) != 0) { kq = 1 - kind; }
    const pm : bool = kq == 1;
    const tqd : []const u32 = sq_qd_tab(kq);
    const tqg : []const u32 = sq_qg_tab(kq);
    const closed : bool = (mode & SQ_M_NOCLOSURE) == 0;
    const qd : u64 = sq_qt(tqd, x, xn, y, pm);
    const qg : u64 = sq_qt(tqg, x, xn, y, pm);
    var qs : u64 = sc_flip(sc_sadd(qd, qg));
    if (closed) { qs = sq_qsrc(qd, qg, sq_qt(tqd, x, xn, 0, pm), sq_qt(tqg, x, xn, 0, pm), sq_qt(tqd, 0, 0, y, pm), sq_qt(tqg, 0, 0, y, pm)); }
    const mq : u64 = m * SQ_QS;
    var nd : u32 = hi;
    var ns : u32 = lo;
    if (kind == 1) {
        nd = lo;
        ns = hi;
    }
    sq_acc(qa, nd, sq_mul(qd, mq));
    sq_acc(qa, g, sq_mul(qg, mq));
    sq_acc(qa, ns, sq_mul(qs, mq));
    if (!jac) { return; }
    const dxd : u64 = sq_mul(sq_slope(tqd, x, y, 0, pm), mq);
    const dyd : u64 = sq_mul(sq_slope(tqd, x, y, 1, pm), mq);
    const dxg : u64 = sq_mul(sq_slope(tqg, x, y, 0, pm), mq);
    const dyg : u64 = sq_mul(sq_slope(tqg, x, y, 1, pm), mq);
    var sxs : u64 = sc_flip(sc_sadd(dxd, dxg));
    var sys : u64 = sc_flip(sc_sadd(dyd, dyg));
    if (closed) {
        sxs = sq_mul(sq_qsrc(sq_slope(tqd, x, y, 0, pm), sq_slope(tqg, x, y, 0, pm), sq_slope(tqd, x, 0, 0, pm), sq_slope(tqg, x, 0, 0, pm), 0, 0), mq);
        sys = sq_mul(sq_qsrc(sq_slope(tqd, x, y, 1, pm), sq_slope(tqg, x, y, 1, pm), 0, 0, sq_slope(tqd, 0, y, 1, pm), sq_slope(tqg, 0, y, 1, pm)), mq);
    }
    sq_jq(reg, kind, nd, g, hi, lo, dxd, dyd);
    sq_jq(reg, kind, g, g, hi, lo, dxg, dyg);
    sq_jq(reg, kind, ns, g, hi, lo, sxs, sys);
}

; --- the step -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// The node charges of the state v with the clock clk: words 0 .. 7 positive, 8 .. 15 negative.
pub fn sq_charges(v: []const u32, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, mode: u32, qa: []u64) {
    var reg : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
    var i : usize = 0;
    while (i < 16) {
        qa[i] = 0;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var e : usize = 0;
    while (e < (SC_NDEV as usize)) {
        sq_dev(e, v, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, false, &reg, qa);
        e = e + 1;
    }
}

/// All registers of the Newton system at v for the step from v0 (whose node charges are q0): G = (charge(v) - charge(v0)) + (currents out - currents in), J = dG/dv.
pub fn sq_stamp(v: []const u32, v0: []const u32, q0: []const u64, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, mode: u32, reg: []u64) {
    sc_clear(reg);
    var qa : [16]u64 = [0] ** 16;
    var e : usize = 0;
    while (e < (SC_NDEV as usize)) {
        sq_dev(e, v, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, true, reg, &qa);
        e = e + 1;
    }
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (n < SC_NN) {
        reg[(SC_RGP + n) as usize] = reg[(SC_RGP + n) as usize] + qa[n as usize] + q0[(SC_NN + n) as usize];
        reg[(SC_RGN + n) as usize] = reg[(SC_RGN + n) as usize] + qa[(SC_NN + n) as usize] + q0[n as usize];
        n = n + 1;
    }
    if ((mode & SQ_M_NOCHARGE) != 0) {
        n = 0;
        while (n < SC_NN) {
            sc_stamp_cap(reg, n, SQ_CAP_M4B[n as usize], v[n as usize], v0[n as usize]);
            n = n + 1;
        }
        return;
    }
    sc_stamp_cap(reg, SC_DP, SQ_C4, v[SC_DP as usize], v0[SC_DP as usize]);
    sc_stamp_cap(reg, SC_DN, SQ_C4, v[SC_DN as usize], v0[SC_DN as usize]);
}

/// One Newton iteration on the eight nodes at once.
pub fn sq_iter(v: []u32, v0: []const u32, q0: []const u64, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, mode: u32) {
    var reg : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
    var a : [72]u64 = [0] ** 72;
    var x : [8]u64 = [0] ** 8;
    sq_stamp(v, v0, q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, &reg);
    sc_load(&reg, &a);
    sc_eliminate(&a);
    sc_backsub(&a, &x);
    sc_apply_lim(v, &x, SQ_TOP);
}

/// One backward Euler step to step j from the state in v (updated in place): k Newton iterations, then the residual.
pub fn sq_step(v: []u32, j: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, k: u32, mode: u32, jf: u32) -> u32 {
    var v0 : [8]u32 = [0] ** 8;
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (n < SC_NN) {
        v0[n as usize] = v[n as usize];
        n = n + 1;
    }
    const clk : u32 = sq_clk_at(j, jf);
    var q0 : [16]u64 = [0] ** 16;
    sq_charges(&v0, sq_clk_at(j - 1, jf), vdp, vdn, mode, &q0);
    var i : u32 = 0;
    while (i < k) {
        sq_iter(v, &v0, &q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var reg : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
    sq_stamp(v, &v0, &q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, &reg);
    return sc_resid(&reg);
}

/// The state at rest with the clock low: the supply on ap, an, net2, net3 and n_clkc, ground on dp and dn, net1 one threshold below the higher input (the spec's rest) or, when n1 is not 0, at the
/// word n1 (the node no switch resets floats where the leakage of the pair and of the tail balance).
pub fn sq_rest(vdp: u32, vdn: u32, n1: u32, v: []u32) {
    var top : u32 = vdp;
    if (vdn > vdp) { top = vdn; }
    v[0] = SQ_VDD;
    v[1] = SQ_VDD;
    v[2] = top - SC_VTH_U;
    if (n1 > 0) { v[2] = n1; }
    v[3] = SQ_VDD;
    v[4] = SQ_VDD;
    v[5] = SQ_OFF;
    v[6] = SQ_OFF;
    v[7] = SQ_VDD;
}

/// The run: n steps from rest, the inputs 0.75 V + h and 0.75 V - h (exchanged when swap). out gets the 8 nodes of every state, step 0 first; res the residual of every step. Returns the
/// order-sensitive fold of every sample.
pub fn sq_run(h: u32, swap: bool, k: u32, n: u32, mode: u32, n1: u32, jf: u32, out: []u32, res: []u32) -> u64 {
    var vdp : u32 = SQ_OFF + SC_VCM + h;
    var vdn : u32 = SQ_OFF + SC_VCM - h;
    if (swap) {
        vdp = SQ_OFF + SC_VCM - h;
        vdn = SQ_OFF + SC_VCM + h;
    }
    var v : [8]u32 = [0] ** 8;
    sq_rest(vdp, vdn, n1, &v);
    var s : u64 = 0;
    var i : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SC_NN) {
        out[i as usize] = v[i as usize];
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var j : u32 = 1;
    while (j <= n) {
        res[(j - 1) as usize] = sq_step(&v, j, vdp, vdn, k, mode, jf);
        i = 0;
        while (i < SC_NN) {
            out[(j * SC_NN + i) as usize] = v[i as usize];
            s = fold(s, v[i as usize]);
            i = i + 1;
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    return s;
}

/// The time, in steps with SC_QB fractional bits, of the first rising crossing of the level lvl (words) by node sel over n steps, linear between samples; SC_NONE when there is none.
pub fn sq_cross(out: []const u32, sel: u32, n: u32, lvl: u32) -> u32 {
    var j : u32 = 1;
    while (j <= n) {
        const y0 : u32 = out[((j - 1) * SC_NN + sel) as usize];
        const y1 : u32 = out[(j * SC_NN + sel) as usize];
        if (y0 < lvl and y1 >= lvl) {
            const frac : u64 = (((lvl - y0) as u64) << SC_QB) / ((y1 - y0) as u64);
            return ((j - 1) << SC_QB) + (frac as u32);
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    return SC_NONE;
}

/// The decision time: the first output through 0.75 V, in steps with SC_QB fractional bits after the clock's 50 % point; SC_NONE when neither output gets there.
pub fn sq_t_first(out: []const u32, n: u32) -> u32 {
    const lvl : u32 = SQ_OFF + SC_VCM;
    const tp : u32 = sq_cross(out, SC_DP, n, lvl);
    const tn : u32 = sq_cross(out, SC_DN, n, lvl);
    var t : u32 = tp;
    if (tn < tp) { t = tn; }
    if (t == SC_NONE) { return SC_NONE; }
    return t - ((SQ_R << SC_QB) >> 1);
}

/// Is dp above dn in the last state: the decision "VDP > VDN".
pub fn sq_sign(out: []const u32, n: u32) -> bool {
    return out[(n * SC_NN + SC_DP) as usize] > out[(n * SC_NN + SC_DN) as usize];
}

/// The resolution time: |dp - dn| through 0.75 V, in steps with SC_QB fractional bits after the clock's 50 % point; SC_NONE when it does not get there.
pub fn sq_t_res(out: []const u32, n: u32) -> u32 {
    var j : u32 = 1;
    while (j <= n) {
        const y0 : u32 = mag_diff(out[((j - 1) * SC_NN + SC_DP) as usize], out[((j - 1) * SC_NN + SC_DN) as usize]);
        const y1 : u32 = mag_diff(out[(j * SC_NN + SC_DP) as usize], out[(j * SC_NN + SC_DN) as usize]);
        if (y0 < SC_VCM and y1 >= SC_VCM) {
            const frac : u64 = (((SC_VCM - y0) as u64) << SC_QB) / ((y1 - y0) as u64);
            return ((j - 1) << SC_QB) + (frac as u32) - ((SQ_R << SC_QB) >> 1);
        }
        j = j + 1;
    }
    return SC_NONE;
}

/// A time in steps with SC_QB fractional bits, in ps.
pub fn sq_ps(tq: u32) -> f64 {
    return ((tq as f64) / 4096.0) * ((SQ_DT_FS as f64) / 1000.0);
}

/// A node voltage of a run in V: the word less the ground offset.
pub fn sq_volts(w: u32) -> f64 {
    return ((w as f64) - (SQ_OFF as f64)) / 16777216.0;
}

/// The voltage of node i, in V, tps picoseconds after the clock's 50 % point (half a step into the run), linear between the steps of a run.
pub fn sq_node_at(out: []const u32, tps: f64, i: u32) -> f64 {
    const dt : f64 = (SQ_DT_FS as f64) / 1000.0;
    const x : f64 = (tps + dt * (SQ_R as f64) / 2.0) / dt;
    const j0 : u32 = x as u32;
    const f : f64 = x - (j0 as f64);
    const a : f64 = sq_volts(out[(j0 * SC_NN + i) as usize]);
    const b : f64 = sq_volts(out[((j0 + 1) * SC_NN + i) as usize]);
    return a + f * (b - a);
}

/// The largest distance, in V, of the run's nodes from the reference rows ng (row r: the eight nodes ap an net1 net2 net3 dp dn n_clkc at tps[r] ps after the clock's 50 % point), rows first .. last - 1.
pub fn sq_node_err(out: []const u32, ng: []const f64, tps: []const f64, first: u32, last: u32) -> f64 {
    var worst : f64 = 0.0;
    var r : u32 = first;
    while (r < last) {
        var i : u32 = 0;
        while (i < SC_NN) {
            const d : f64 = fabs64(sq_node_at(out, tps[r as usize], i) - ng[(r * SC_NN + i) as usize]);
            if (d > worst) { worst = d; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        r = r + 1;
    }
    return worst;
}

/// A signed word as a real.
pub fn sq_wf(w: u64) -> f64 {
    if (sc_neg(w)) { return 0.0 - (sc_mag(w) as f64); }
    return (sc_mag(w) as f64);
}

/// The residual of node n of a stamp in words (positive terms less negative), and the Jacobian entry (r, c).
pub fn sq_gword(reg: []const u64, n: u32) -> f64 {
    return ((reg[(SC_RGP + n) as usize]) as f64) - ((reg[(SC_RGN + n) as usize]) as f64);
}

pub fn sq_jword(reg: []const u64, r: u32, c: u32) -> f64 {
    return ((reg[(SC_RJP + r * SC_NN + c) as usize]) as f64) - ((reg[(SC_RJN + r * SC_NN + c) as usize]) as f64);
}

/// The Jacobian of the stamp at v (for the step from v0, the clock going from clk0 to clk) against the central differences of its residual over dl units of each node: the largest
/// |J - difference| over the 64 entries, each as a fraction of the diagonal of its row (with transposed the Jacobian is read as its transpose: the negative control).
pub fn sq_jac_err(v: []const u32, v0: []const u32, clk0: u32, clk: u32, vdp: u32, vdn: u32, mode: u32, dl: u32, transposed: bool) -> f64 {
    var q0 : [16]u64 = [0] ** 16;
    sq_charges(v0, clk0, vdp, vdn, mode, &q0);
    var reg : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
    sq_stamp(v, v0, &q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, &reg);
    var worst : f64 = 0.0;
    var c : u32 = 0;
    while (c < SC_NN) {
        var vp : [8]u32 = [0] ** 8;
        var vm : [8]u32 = [0] ** 8;
        var i : usize = 0;
        while (i < 8) {
            vp[i] = v[i];
            vm[i] = v[i];
            i = i + 1;
        }
        vp[c as usize] = v[c as usize] + dl;
        vm[c as usize] = v[c as usize] - dl;
        var rp : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
        var rm : [144]u64 = [0] ** 144;
        sq_stamp(&vp, v0, &q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, &rp);
        sq_stamp(&vm, v0, &q0, clk, vdp, vdn, mode, &rm);
        var r : u32 = 0;
        while (r < SC_NN) {
            const fd : f64 = ((sq_gword(&rp, r) - sq_gword(&rm, r)) / (2.0 * (dl as f64))) * 1048576.0;
            var ja : f64 = sq_jword(&reg, r, c);
            if (transposed) { ja = sq_jword(&reg, c, r); }
            const e : f64 = fabs64(ja - fd) / fabs64(sq_jword(&reg, r, r));
            if (e > worst) { worst = e; }
            r = r + 1;
        }
        c = c + 1;
    }
    return worst;
}

; --- what ngspice-47 printed ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The decks are specs/analog/decks/sar_cmp_q_ref.cir, sar_cmp_q_ref50.cir, sar_cmp_q_free.cir and sar_cmp_q_be.cir, run on the reference host (a container, 2 threads), 2026-10-20, ngspice-47, PSP103
; of the IHP-Open-PDK 21133f21, mos_tt; the numbers are the printed ones, none changed (a time is tfirst less tck, the 6 digits printed).
/// The decision time of the golden comparator, ngspice-47 PSP103 tt 27 C, the SETTLED start (sar_cmp_q_ref.cir RUN S): the first output through 0.75 V after the clock's 50 percent point, ps, for h = 16777 4194 1049 262 84 8 1.
